## Context

Reading-1 item 14 said "Em-dashes are an AI tell — sweep and restyle
(abstract and body)." Ticket 0543 (PR #992) verified the body and
abstract carry zero *Unicode* em dashes and waived the sweep on that
basis. The PR #992 prose-review panel pointed out the gap: the LaTeX
`---` idiom renders as an em dash in the PDF the author annotated, and
`slides/manuscript/main.tex` carries ~187 `---` occurrences in body
prose. From the reader's side, item 14 is not resolved; from the
source side, `---` may be a deliberate typographic convention.

Restyling ~187 sites is an authorial-voice decision, out of scope for
an autonomous editorial pass (several sit near test-pinned strings).

## Actions

1. Author decides: (a) `---` is house style, item 14 was about Unicode
   tells only — close this ticket with a waiver note; or (b) sweep and
   restyle `---` in body prose (commas, colons, parentheses, sentence
   splits), excluding quoted material (the verbatim Doc-07 prompt
   block) and table/figure syntax.
2. If (b): execute as its own PR; extend the abstract em-dash guard in
   `tests/test_manuscript_cohort_and_caveats.py` to body prose,
   excluding quote environments.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Author decision recorded in this log
- [ ] Sweep executed or waiver noted; `make check` green
